# @boundary rejects '5_i7' has no type: an integer suffix is _i or _u, alone or with 8, 16, 32, 64 or 128 bits
#
# A width Zebra has no type for is refused by name, never passed through to Zig (which
# would accept `i7`). Written before the feature was built (2026-11-05).
def main()
    var x = 5_i7
    print(x)
